IMPORT prelude

-- Land Acquisition Act 1966 (Singapore) -- compensation for compulsorily acquired land: the matters to be considered (s 33) and the
-- matters to be disregarded (s 34).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LAA1966.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 13 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the compensation rules. Not encoded:
-- the notification and declaration procedure (ss 3 to 8), the Collector's inquiry and award, the Appeals Board and its procedure,
-- taking possession, temporary occupation, and the airspace and subterranean provisions beyond their compensation heads.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Land Acquisition Act 1966 -- compensation`

§§ `33(1)(a), (6) -- the valuation date`

-- s 33(1)(a): market value (i) as at the date of the s 3(1) notification, if that notification is followed WITHIN 6 MONTHS by a s 5
-- declaration for the same land; or (ii) otherwise as at the date of the s 5 declaration.
GIVEN `months from notification to declaration` IS A NUMBER, `there was a section 3 notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`the valuation date` MEANS
    IF `there was a section 3 notification` AND `months from notification to declaration` AT MOST 6
    THEN "the date of the section 3 notification"
    ELSE "the date of the section 5 declaration"

§§ `33(5) -- caps on market value`

-- (5)(b): any increase in value from a use that could be restrained by a court, is unlawful, or is detrimental to health is ignored.
-- (5)(d): if the owner stated a value for tax or duty within 2 years before the s 5 declaration and it was accepted, the market
-- value "is deemed not to exceed" that value.
-- (5)(e): market value is deemed not to exceed what a bona fide purchaser would pay given the zoning, density and other Planning
-- Act restrictions, and "no account is to be taken of any potential value of the land for any other use more intensive than that
-- permitted".
DECLARE Valuation HAS
    `market value at current zoning` IS A NUMBER
    `value with hope of rezoning` IS A NUMBER
    `value declared for tax within 2 years` IS A NUMBER
    `there is such a tax declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uplift from unlawful use` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF a LESS THAN b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN `the valuation` IS A Valuation
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the market value allowed` MEANS
    IF `the valuation`'s `there is such a tax declaration`
    THEN `the lesser of` (`the valuation`'s `market value at current zoning` MINUS `the valuation`'s `uplift from unlawful use`) (`the valuation`'s `value declared for tax within 2 years`)
    ELSE `the valuation`'s `market value at current zoning` MINUS `the valuation`'s `uplift from unlawful use`

§§ `33(1)(b)-(f), 33(2) -- the other heads`

-- s 33(1): the Board considers "the following matters and NO OTHERS": (a) market value; (b) betterment of the owner's other land;
-- (c) severance damage; (d) injurious affection to other property; (e) reasonable expenses of a compelled change of residence or
-- business; (f) costs of reissuing title.
-- s 33(2): betterment of the owner's other land "is to be set off ONLY against" severance and injurious-affection damages -- never
-- against market value or the relocation and title costs.
DECLARE Claim HAS
    `market value allowed` IS A NUMBER
    `severance damage` IS A NUMBER
    `injurious affection` IS A NUMBER
    `betterment to other land` IS A NUMBER
    `relocation expenses` IS A NUMBER
    `title costs` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation` MEANS
        `the claim`'s `market value allowed`
    PLUS (IF `the claim`'s `severance damage` PLUS `the claim`'s `injurious affection` GREATER THAN `the claim`'s `betterment to other land`
          THEN `the claim`'s `severance damage` PLUS `the claim`'s `injurious affection` MINUS `the claim`'s `betterment to other land`
          ELSE 0)
    PLUS `the claim`'s `relocation expenses`
    PLUS `the claim`'s `title costs`

§§ `34 -- matters disregarded`

-- s 34: the Board "must not take into consideration" (a) urgency; (b) the owner's disinclination to part with the land; (c) damage
-- not actionable against a private person; (d) damage from the future use; (e) increase in value from the future use; (f) outlay on
-- improvements AFTER the s 5 notification unless needed for repair and approved by the Commissioner of Lands; (g) evidence of a
-- transaction not stamped, registered and filed 6 months before the notification; (h) comparable sales, unless the Board is
-- satisfied they were bona fide and not speculative -- "the ONUS ... shall lie with the APPELLANT".
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `the owner's reluctance to sell`
    `the urgency of the project`
    `the value the project will add to the acquired land`
    `a renovation done after the notification`
    `a repair after the notification approved by the Commissioner of Lands`
    `a comparable sale proved bona fide by the appellant`
    `a comparable sale not proved bona fide`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may take the matter into account` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `a repair after the notification approved by the Commissioner of Lands` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a comparable sale proved bona fide by the appellant` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
